          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 cannot light because their common anode net is floating. This would disable the associated Ethernet/activity LED functions while leaving the rest of the board electrically similar.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a connectivity anomaly: the LED power net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW is connected only to the anodes of D4, D14, and D23 and is not connected to any 3.3 V source or driver, so those LEDs cannot operate as intended."
}

